<title>KAZAKHSTAN: TABLE-Kazakh 3-mth T-bill yield firms to 13.56 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Kazakh 3-mth T-bill yield firms to 13.56 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills edged up to 13.56 percent annual at an auction on Tuesday from 13.44 percent at the last auction on July 15, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   July 22	    July 15</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K2310979     KZ43K1610973</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  500		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 1,283		1,197</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 501		  506</p>
<p> Average price			 96.72 pct	  96.75</p>
<p> Average yield			 13.56 pct	  13.44 pct</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Oct 23, 1997     Oct 16, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
</text>
